   {
    "title": "📑 Chapter 00-Course Introduction (15 slides)|||📑 Chapter 00-Course Introduction (15 slide)",
    "slug": "prn232-flm-slide-d01",
    "type": "DOCUMENT",
    "description": "15 slide",
    "content": "<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/001.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 1: Building Cross-Platform Back-End Application with .NET (PRN232)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 1/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Building Cross-Platform Back-End Application with .NET (PRN232)</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/002.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 2: Why should you study this course?\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 2/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Why should you study this course?<br>‹#›<br>Apply C# language for develop ASP.NET WEB API ( RESTful Service applications )<br>Understand fundamental concepts of .NET Core Platform<br>Understand the basic knowledge of  ASP.NET WEB API on .NET Core<br>Understand the basic knowledge of RESTful Service and Microservice architecture</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/003.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 3: Completed:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 3/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Completed:<br>PRN222 (Building Cross-Platform Web Application With .NET)<br>‹#›<br>Prerequisites</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/004.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 4: Course Objectives\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 4/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Objectives<br>Describe about  .NET Core Platform,  and ASP.NET Core Web API, ASP.NET Core Web API with OData<br>Demonstrate Models, Media Formatters &amp; Content Negotiation in Web API<br>Demonstrate about  and Binding, Validation &amp; Routing and sending AJAX Requests to ASP.NET Core Web API<br>Demonstrate about implementing security in RESTful WebService, implementing RESTful Services by WCF, gRPC Services and introduction about Microservices architecture.<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/005.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 5: Course Description\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 5/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Description<br>Develop Cross - platform Back-end application can be used by  Desktop or Web applications (Cross - platform)<br>Develop RESTful Service applications by ASP.NET Web API  and Windows Communication Foundation (WCF), gPRC<br>Implement  security in the ASP.NET Core Web API using JWT<br>Implement sending Ajax request to  ASP.NET Core Web API<br>Introduce about developing the distributed applications based on Microservice architecture<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/006.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 6: Course Plan\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 6/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Plan<br>See course plan on CMS<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/007.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 7: Materials/ References\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 7/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Materials/ References<br>1. C# 12 in a Nutshell<br>2. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/ef/core/<br>3. C# 12 and .NET 8 – Modern Cross-Platform Development Fundamentals&quot;<br>4. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/introduction<br>5. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/whats-new/csharp-12<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/008.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 8: Learning Environments\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 8/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Learning Environments<br>.NET 8 or later<br>Visual Studio 2022 or later (https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/downloads/)<br>MS SQL Server 2016 or later<br>A Notebook for reports of labs and assignments.<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/009.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 9: Course Rules\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 9/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Rules<br>How to conduct<br>Prepare contents of the next session at home<br>Following lessons in classroom<br>Completing chapter assessments in time and Quizzes (via CMS)<br>Write reports of all labs and assignments to your notebook<br>Communication<br>Class - Interchange by FU-HCM LMS, Forum<br>Discussing actively in your team and classroom.<br>Free to ask questions<br>Others<br>Off phone, no game, no chat in class<br>Use laptop under teacher’s instruction<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/010.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 10: Evaluation Strategy\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 10/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Evaluation Strategy<br>Must attend at least 80% of contact hours (if not, not allow to take exam).<br>Evaluating<br>02 Progress Tests (PT, 5%) + 02 Assignments (AS, 15%)<br>01 Practical Exam (PE, 25%)  + 01 Group Project (GP, 25%)<br>Final Exam (FE, 30%)<br>Total score=10%(PT)+10%(AS)+25%(PE)+25%(GR)+30% (FE)<br>Pass:<br>Every on-going assessment component &gt;0 and Practical Exam &gt;=4 and Final Exam Score &gt;=4 and Final Result  &gt;=5<br>Final exam retake only when not passed<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/011.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 11: How to study (1)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 11/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>How to study (1)<br>This course is complex knowledge (however, it’s attractive and exciting), so you need to keep a tight grip on it<br>Read<br>On the books to get the general concept<br>Reference, study, collection from anywhere else (internet, your classmate, forum …)<br>Attend lectures<br>Listen, understand, then make your notes<br>Give your explanation about some topic in lectures. Ask questions<br>Give some examples that do not exist in your book<br>Practice all the exercises, demo to make your sense<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/012.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 12: How to study (2)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 12/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>How to study (2)<br>After classes<br>Discuss your classmate indirectly, on the forum<br>Analyze, design, and implement workshops and assignments.<br>Write reports in your notebook<br>Build your team in yourselves to support together in studying<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/013.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 13: Academic policy\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 13/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Academic policy<br>Cheating, plagiarism and breach of copyright are serious offenses under this Policy.<br>Cheating<br>Cheating during a test or exam is construed as talking, peeking at another student’s paper or any other clandestine method of transmitting information.<br>Plagiarism<br>Plagiarism is using the work of others without citing it; that is, holding the work of others out as your own work.<br>Breach of Copyright<br>If you photocopy a textbook without the copyright holder's permission, you violate copyright law.<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/014.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 14: Enjoy the Course\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 14/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Enjoy the Course<br>Be enthusiastic about the material because it is interesting, useful and an important part of your training as a software engineer.<br>Our job is to help you learn and enjoy the experience.<br>We will do our best but we need your help.<br>So let’s all have fun together with C# Application Development!!!<br>‹#›</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/PRN232/flm1/d01/015.webp\" alt=\"PRN232 · Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 15: Q&amp;A\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 00-Course Introduction · slide 15/15</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Q&amp;A<br>‹#›</p></div>"
   }
